{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "worldpop_u18_2025_total",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Estimated number of children under 18 per ~100 m grid cell in 2025 (WorldPop R2025A, constrained), one item per country.\n\nEstimated number of children under 18 per ~100 m grid cell (3 arc-seconds) in 2025, from the WorldPop R2025A constrained (`CN`) population estimates. Constrained means people are only allocated to cells mapped as built settlement; all other cells are nodata.\n\nThe data are one Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF per country, served from their original location on Azure, with one STAC item per country. The `mosaic` asset of each group is a GDAL VRT over all country files, for global access with a single URL.\n\nUnits: people per grid cell. Nodata: -99999. License: CC-BY-4.0. Citation: WorldPop (www.worldpop.org), R2025A.",
